  "worked_solution": "The operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}$ means that we need to multiply the third row of the matrix by $\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nMultiplying the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{3}$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 6 & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 9 & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
